WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.400
An antibody grips its target, an antigen,

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.690
the way a key fits a lock.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.110
This year's flu virus carries
antigens your body has never met.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.380
Yet within days, your body is
making antibodies that fit them.

5
00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.540
How can your body make antibodies
for a shape it has never seen?

6
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.110
In this mission, you'll
meet the lymphocytes,

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.360
B cells and T cells, that
drive the specific response.

8
00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.500
Then you'll find out why the
first response takes days,

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.840
and why you feel ill while you wait.

10
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:36.040
Your mission: explain how your body makes
antibodies that fit a virus it has never

11
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:36.680
met.
